# Real goblet chain: one site on each radical head (the radical carbon of the drawing)
# and one on the backbone edge opposite each goblet. Generated with the site builder.
# With nearest neighbours only the radical states decouple (tau = 0: flat bands at E_F)
# and the backbone is a uniform chain; t2, t3 add a small tip - backbone coupling.
bands -1 2
site Tu near  3.689   1.42     # radical carbon of the up-goblet head
site Td near 12.298 -24.85     # radical carbon of the down-goblet head
site Bu near  3.689 -14.20     # backbone bottom edge under the up-goblet
site Bd near 12.298  -9.23     # backbone top edge above the down-goblet
onsite Tu eT
onsite Td eT
onsite Bu eB
onsite Bd eB
hop Bu Bd 0 tB                 # uniform backbone chain (the goblets are evenly spaced)
hop Bd Bu 1 tB
hop Tu Bu 0 tau                # each head couples to the backbone under its own goblet
hop Td Bd 0 tau
